<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-market, intervention grains.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-market, intervention grains.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following exports of free market and intervention grains, traders said.</p>
<p>			   Tonnage	   Maximum refund (Ecus/tonne)</p>
<p>MAIN TENDER</p>
<p>    Soft wheat	 332,500		 6.90</p>
<p>    Barley		63,500		31.00</p>
<p>    Rye		    5,150		30.09</p>
<p>    Oats		  22,000		30.59</p>
<p>TENDER FOR EXPORT TO ACP COUNTRIES</p>
<p>    Soft wheat	  21,000		12.00</p>
<p>INTERVENTION TENDER</p>
<p>			   TONNAGE	   MINIMUM PRICE (Ecus/tonne)</p>
<p>    German barley     24,776	     104.53 Ecus minimum price</p>
<p>    German rye	  25,392	     100.52 Ecus minimum price</p>
</text>
